IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g4-interpretation`
IMPORT `g4-nouns`
IMPORT `g4-art11-application`

-- g4-art11-decision.l4: Article 11 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, paragraphs (4) to (7) and (9): the six matters, the duty to register and the duty to refuse, the guidance on a substantial
-- activity, the grounds the States may add, and the certificates. Paragraphs (1) to (3), (8), (10) and (11) are in g4-art11-application.l4.
-- Time. Part 4 (Articles 8 to 17) came into force on 1 May 2018 (R&O.17/2018); whether it is in force on a day is the integrator's wrapper, not a gate here (PLAN section 10). No entry in the Table of Endnote References
-- amends Articles 11 or 12, so one text of them is encoded for every vintage; only the identity of "the Minister" (Article 1) varies by vintage, and the rules here are typed by the ROLE `the Minister`.
-- Facts that another group decides come in as the standard inputs of PLAN section (c), under their exact names, and are never computed here: IP8 (the charity test), IP17 (the principal address),
-- IP18 (a name undesirable under Article 12(1)), IP22 (Article 19(5)), IP23 (Article 19(9)(c)), IP24 (a court order not to register), IP29 (an Order under Article 13(9)).
-- The Commissioner's "satisfied" is not a further input: each of the six matters is supplied as the Commissioner's finding on it (the opinion of (c)(ii), the finding of IP8, IP17 and IP18, the grounds of (f)).

§ `Part 4 -- Charity register`

§§ `Article 11 -- Application to register (continued)`

§§§ `Article 11(4) -- the six matters`

-- src:320 | (a) the applicant meets the charity test, or will do so on registration;
@ref Article 11(4)(a) (src:320)
GIVEN
  `the entity meets the charity test` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 5: whether the applicant meets the charity test now
  `the findings` IS A `Findings of the Commissioner for Article 11(4)` @desc The Commissioner's findings on the matters of Article 11(4) that no other group decides, and on the grounds prescribed under Article 11(7)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 11(4)(a) the applicant meets the charity test, or will do so on registration` IF
        `the entity meets the charity test`
    OR  `the findings`'s `applicant will meet the charity test on registration`

-- src:321 | (b) the constitution of the applicant is a written document;
@ref Article 11(4)(b) (src:321)
GIVEN
  `the findings` IS A `Findings of the Commissioner for Article 11(4)` @desc The Commissioner's findings on the matters of Article 11(4) that no other group decides, and on the grounds prescribed under Article 11(7)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 11(4)(b) the constitution of the applicant is a written document` IF
    `the findings`'s `constitution of the applicant is a written document`

-- src:322 | (c) the applicant –
-- src:323 | (i) is a Jersey entity, or
@ref Article 11(4)(c)(i) (src:322-323)
GIVEN
  `the entity` IS AN Entity @desc The applicant as Article 2 leaves it: its kinds of entity, whether it is a Jersey entity, its governors and its purposes
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 11(4)(c)(i) the applicant is a Jersey entity` IF
    `the entity`'s `is a Jersey entity`

-- src:322 | (c) the applicant –
-- src:324 | (ii) carries out, or intends to carry out, in or from within Jersey, an activity that is, in the opinion of the Commissioner, substantial;
@ref Article 11(4)(c)(ii) (src:322) (src:324)
GIVEN `the applicant carries out, or intends to carry out, an activity in or from within Jersey` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the applicant carries out, or intends to carry out, an activity in or from within Jersey
      `the activity is, in the opinion of the Commissioner, substantial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The Commissioner's opinion that the activity is substantial; the Commissioner must have regard to the guidance of Article 11(6) in forming it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 11(4)(c)(ii) the applicant carries out an activity that is substantial` IF
        `the applicant carries out, or intends to carry out, an activity in or from within Jersey`
    AND `the activity is, in the opinion of the Commissioner, substantial`

-- src:322 | (c) the applicant –
-- src:323 | (i) is a Jersey entity, or
-- src:324 | (ii) carries out, or intends to carry out, in or from within Jersey, an activity that is, in the opinion of the Commissioner, substantial;
@ref Article 11(4)(c) (src:322-324)
@export Whether the requirement of Article 11(4)(c) is met: the entity is a Jersey entity, or it carries out, or intends to carry out, in or from within Jersey an activity that is, in the Commissioner's opinion, substantial (standard fact IP15)
GIVEN
  `the entity` IS AN Entity @desc The applicant as Article 2 leaves it: its kinds of entity, whether it is a Jersey entity, its governors and its purposes
  `the applicant carries out, or intends to carry out, an activity in or from within Jersey` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the entity carries out, or intends to carry out, an activity in or from within Jersey
  `the activity is, in the opinion of the Commissioner, substantial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The Commissioner's opinion that the activity is substantial
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 11(4)(c) the requirement is met` IF
        `Art 11(4)(c)(i) the applicant is a Jersey entity` `the entity`
    OR  `Art 11(4)(c)(ii) the applicant carries out an activity that is substantial` `the applicant carries out, or intends to carry out, an activity in or from within Jersey` `the activity is, in the opinion of the Commissioner, substantial`

-- src:325 | (d) the applicant has a principal address in Jersey, within the meaning of Article 8(4);
@ref Article 11(4)(d) (src:325)
@export Whether the requirement of Article 11(4)(d) is met: the entity has a principal address in Jersey, within the meaning of Article 8(4) (standard fact IP16)
GIVEN
  `the entity has a principal address in Jersey within Article 8(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the applicant has a principal address in Jersey within the meaning of Article 8(4)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 11(4)(d) the requirement is met` IF
    `the entity has a principal address in Jersey within Article 8(4)`

-- src:326 | (e) the name of the applicant is not undesirable under Article 12; and
@ref Article 11(4)(e) (src:326)
GIVEN
  `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the name of the applicant is, in the Commissioner's opinion, undesirable as the registered name of a charity on a ground in Article 12(1)(a) to (d)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 11(4)(e) the name of the applicant is not undesirable under Article 12` IF
    NOT `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1)`

-- (f): "no other ground for refusal, prescribed under paragraph (7), applies or should be applied". F4.12. Reading A: a ground on which an application MUST be refused "applies"; a ground on which it MAY be refused
-- "should be applied" when the Commissioner so considers (the words of Article 9(6)(c) are the same in more words). Reading B: any prescribed ground whose circumstances are present defeats the matter.
-- The grounds are in Regulations that are not among the sources, so every fact about them is an input.
-- src:327 | (f) no other ground for refusal, prescribed under paragraph (7), applies or should be applied.
@ref Article 11(4)(f) (src:327)
GIVEN
  `the findings` IS A `Findings of the Commissioner for Article 11(4)` @desc The Commissioner's findings on the matters of Article 11(4) that no other group decides, and on the grounds prescribed under Article 11(7)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `F4.12 reading A: no ground of mandatory refusal applies and no ground of discretionary refusal should be applied` IF
    NOT (   `the findings`'s `a ground prescribed under Article 11(7) on which the application must be refused applies`
         OR `the findings`'s `a ground prescribed under Article 11(7) on which the application may be refused should be applied` )

-- src:327 | (f) no other ground for refusal, prescribed under paragraph (7), applies or should be applied.
@ref Article 11(4)(f) (src:327)
GIVEN
  `the findings` IS A `Findings of the Commissioner for Article 11(4)` @desc The Commissioner's findings on the matters of Article 11(4) that no other group decides, and on the grounds prescribed under Article 11(7)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `F4.12 reading B: no prescribed ground has its circumstances present` IF
    NOT (   `the findings`'s `a ground prescribed under Article 11(7) on which the application must be refused applies`
         OR `the findings`'s `a ground prescribed under Article 11(7) on which the application may be refused has its circumstances present`
         OR `the findings`'s `a ground prescribed under Article 11(7) on which the application may be refused should be applied` )

-- src:327 | (f) no other ground for refusal, prescribed under paragraph (7), applies or should be applied.
@ref Article 11(4)(f) (src:327)
GIVEN
  interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 11 and 12` @desc The reading of each ambiguity of Articles 11 and 12; a field left out takes the reading the encoding takes (see the fork register in FRAGMENT-G4.md)
  `the findings` IS A `Findings of the Commissioner for Article 11(4)` @desc The Commissioner's findings on the matters of Article 11(4) that no other group decides, and on the grounds prescribed under Article 11(7)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 11(4)(f) no other ground for refusal prescribed under Article 11(7) applies or should be applied` IF
    CONSIDER interp's `how applies or should be applied is read in Article 11(4)(f)`
    WHEN `a ground of mandatory refusal applies, or a ground of discretionary refusal should be applied` THEN `F4.12 reading A: no ground of mandatory refusal applies and no ground of discretionary refusal should be applied` `the findings`
    WHEN `any prescribed ground whose circumstances are present defeats the matter` THEN `F4.12 reading B: no prescribed ground has its circumstances present` `the findings`

-- src:319 | (4) If the applicant complies with paragraph (2), with any Regulations under paragraph (3), and with Article 19(5), the Commissioner must register the applicant as a charity if satisfied that –
-- src:320 | (a) the applicant meets the charity test, or will do so on registration;
-- src:321 | (b) the constitution of the applicant is a written document;
-- src:322 | (c) the applicant –
-- src:323 | (i) is a Jersey entity, or
-- src:324 | (ii) carries out, or intends to carry out, in or from within Jersey, an activity that is, in the opinion of the Commissioner, substantial;
-- src:325 | (d) the applicant has a principal address in Jersey, within the meaning of Article 8(4);
-- src:326 | (e) the name of the applicant is not undesirable under Article 12; and
-- src:327 | (f) no other ground for refusal, prescribed under paragraph (7), applies or should be applied.
@ref Article 11(4) (src:319-327)
GIVEN
  interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 11 and 12` @desc The reading of each ambiguity of Articles 11 and 12; a field left out takes the reading the encoding takes (see the fork register in FRAGMENT-G4.md)
  `the application` IS AN `Application for registration` @desc What the applicant has provided under Article 11(2), with the day it was lodged and the day, if any, it became complete
  `an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an Order under Article 13(9)(b) requires a registered charity to give a statement of its intentions about payments to governors; Article 11(2)(e)(ii) reads it of the applicant as it would be once registered
  `the applicant has complied with Article 19(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the application states that the entity holds declarations from all its governors who have not made a report under Article 19(2)
  `the entity` IS AN Entity @desc The applicant as Article 2 leaves it: its kinds of entity, whether it is a Jersey entity, its governors and its purposes
  `the entity meets the charity test` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 5: whether the applicant meets the charity test now
  `the findings` IS A `Findings of the Commissioner for Article 11(4)` @desc The Commissioner's findings on the matters of Article 11(4) that no other group decides, and on the grounds prescribed under Article 11(7)
  `the entity has a principal address in Jersey within Article 8(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the applicant has a principal address in Jersey within the meaning of Article 8(4)
  `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the name of the applicant is, in the Commissioner's opinion, undesirable as the registered name of a charity on a ground in Article 12(1)(a) to (d)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 11(4) the six matters are found` IF
        `Art 11(4)(a) the applicant meets the charity test, or will do so on registration` `the entity meets the charity test` `the findings`
    AND `Art 11(4)(b) the constitution of the applicant is a written document` `the findings`
    AND `Art 11(4)(c) the requirement is met` `the entity` (`the findings`'s `applicant carries out, or intends to carry out, an activity in or from within Jersey`) (`the findings`'s `activity is, in the opinion of the Commissioner, substantial`)
    AND `Art 11(4)(d) the requirement is met` `the entity has a principal address in Jersey within Article 8(4)`
    AND `Art 11(4)(e) the name of the applicant is not undesirable under Article 12` `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1)`
    AND `Art 11(4)(f) no other ground for refusal prescribed under Article 11(7) applies or should be applied` interp `the findings`

-- The chapeau of Article 11(4): "If the applicant complies with paragraph (2), with any Regulations under paragraph (3), and with Article 19(5)". Compliance with paragraph (2) includes what Regulations under (3)(a) require
-- (it is item (f)(i)); the procedure Regulations under (3)(b) may prescribe is a separate fact; Article 19(5) is the standard fact IP22.
-- src:319 | (4) If the applicant complies with paragraph (2), with any Regulations under paragraph (3), and with Article 19(5), the Commissioner must register the applicant as a charity if satisfied that –
@ref Article 11(4) (src:319)
@export Whether the applicant complies with Article 11(2), with any Regulations under Article 11(3) and with Article 19(5), which is the condition on which the duty of Article 11(4) arises
GIVEN
  interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 11 and 12` @desc The reading of each ambiguity of Articles 11 and 12; a field left out takes the reading the encoding takes (see the fork register in FRAGMENT-G4.md)
  `the application` IS AN `Application for registration` @desc What the applicant has provided under Article 11(2), with the day it was lodged and the day, if any, it became complete
  `an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an Order under Article 13(9)(b) requires a registered charity to give a statement of its intentions about payments to governors; Article 11(2)(e)(ii) reads it of the applicant as it would be once registered
  `the applicant has complied with Article 19(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the application states that the entity holds declarations from all its governors who have not made a report under Article 19(2)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 11(4) the applicant has complied with Article 11(2), the Regulations and Article 19(5)` IF
        `Art 11(2) the application includes what Article 11(2) requires` interp `the application` `an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity`
    AND `the application`'s `other requirements under Article 11(2)(f)`'s `procedure under Regulations under Article 11(3)(b) followed`
    AND `the applicant has complied with Article 19(5)`

§§§ `Article 11(4), (5) -- the duty to register and the duty to refuse (trap T10; forks F4.3, F4.4)`

-- F4.3: the duty before the bars of Articles 19(9)(c) and 20(1)(c) are considered. Three readings, each a function of two facts: whether the applicant complies (the chapeau of Article 11(4)),
-- and whether the six matters are found. Reading A: neither duty arises while the application does not comply. Reading B: it must be refused. Reading C: Article 11(5) read on its own words.
-- src:319 | (4) If the applicant complies with paragraph (2), with any Regulations under paragraph (3), and with Article 19(5), the Commissioner must register the applicant as a charity if satisfied that –
-- src:328 | (5) If not so satisfied, the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant.
@ref Article 11(4) and (5) (src:319) (src:328)
GIVEN complies IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the applicant complies with Article 11(2), the Regulations and Article 19(5)
      found IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the six matters of Article 11(4) are found
GIVETH A `Duty of the Commissioner on an application for registration`
DECIDE `F4.3 reading A: a non-complying application leaves the Commissioner with no duty` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT complies THEN `no duty to register or to refuse arises because the application does not comply`
        IF found THEN `the Commissioner must register the applicant`
        OTHERWISE `the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant`

-- src:319 | (4) If the applicant complies with paragraph (2), with any Regulations under paragraph (3), and with Article 19(5), the Commissioner must register the applicant as a charity if satisfied that –
-- src:328 | (5) If not so satisfied, the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant.
@ref Article 11(4) and (5) (src:319) (src:328)
GIVEN complies IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the applicant complies with Article 11(2), the Regulations and Article 19(5)
      found IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the six matters of Article 11(4) are found
GIVETH A `Duty of the Commissioner on an application for registration`
DECIDE `F4.3 reading B: a non-complying application must be refused` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT complies THEN `the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant`
        IF found THEN `the Commissioner must register the applicant`
        OTHERWISE `the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant`

-- src:319 | (4) If the applicant complies with paragraph (2), with any Regulations under paragraph (3), and with Article 19(5), the Commissioner must register the applicant as a charity if satisfied that –
-- src:328 | (5) If not so satisfied, the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant.
@ref Article 11(4) and (5) (src:319) (src:328)
GIVEN complies IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the applicant complies with Article 11(2), the Regulations and Article 19(5)
      found IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the six matters of Article 11(4) are found
GIVETH A `Duty of the Commissioner on an application for registration`
DECIDE `F4.3 reading C: the duty to refuse depends on the six matters alone` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT found THEN `the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant`
        IF complies THEN `the Commissioner must register the applicant`
        OTHERWISE `no duty to register or to refuse arises because the application does not comply`

-- src:319 | (4) If the applicant complies with paragraph (2), with any Regulations under paragraph (3), and with Article 19(5), the Commissioner must register the applicant as a charity if satisfied that –
-- src:328 | (5) If not so satisfied, the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant.
@ref Article 11(4) and (5) (src:319) (src:328)
GIVEN
  interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 11 and 12` @desc The reading of each ambiguity of Articles 11 and 12; a field left out takes the reading the encoding takes (see the fork register in FRAGMENT-G4.md)
  `the application` IS AN `Application for registration` @desc What the applicant has provided under Article 11(2), with the day it was lodged and the day, if any, it became complete
  `an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an Order under Article 13(9)(b) requires a registered charity to give a statement of its intentions about payments to governors; Article 11(2)(e)(ii) reads it of the applicant as it would be once registered
  `the applicant has complied with Article 19(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the application states that the entity holds declarations from all its governors who have not made a report under Article 19(2)
  `the entity` IS AN Entity @desc The applicant as Article 2 leaves it: its kinds of entity, whether it is a Jersey entity, its governors and its purposes
  `the entity meets the charity test` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 5: whether the applicant meets the charity test now
  `the findings` IS A `Findings of the Commissioner for Article 11(4)` @desc The Commissioner's findings on the matters of Article 11(4) that no other group decides, and on the grounds prescribed under Article 11(7)
  `the entity has a principal address in Jersey within Article 8(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the applicant has a principal address in Jersey within the meaning of Article 8(4)
  `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the name of the applicant is, in the Commissioner's opinion, undesirable as the registered name of a charity on a ground in Article 12(1)(a) to (d)
  `Article 19(9)(c) bars granting the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a reported fitness issue about a governor is undetermined, or its resulting order or notice has not been complied with
  `the court has ordered that the entity must not be registered as a charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has made an order under Article 20(1)(c) that the entity must not be registered as a charity
GIVETH A `Duty of the Commissioner on an application for registration`
DECIDE `Art 11 the duty before the bars on granting` IS
    CONSIDER interp's `what an application that does not comply leads to`
    WHEN `no duty to register or to refuse arises while the application does not comply` THEN `F4.3 reading A: a non-complying application leaves the Commissioner with no duty` complies found
    WHEN `the Commissioner must refuse an application that does not comply` THEN `F4.3 reading B: a non-complying application must be refused` complies found
    WHEN `the duty to refuse depends on the six matters alone` THEN `F4.3 reading C: the duty to refuse depends on the six matters alone` complies found
    WHERE
        complies MEANS `Art 11(4) the applicant has complied with Article 11(2), the Regulations and Article 19(5)` interp `the application` `an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity` `the applicant has complied with Article 19(5)`
        found MEANS `Art 11(4) the six matters are found` interp `the application` `an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity` `the applicant has complied with Article 19(5)` `the entity` `the entity meets the charity test` `the findings` `the entity has a principal address in Jersey within Article 8(4)` `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1)`

-- F4.4: the duty to register against the bars. Article 19(9)(c): the Commissioner "must not, in the case of an application for registration, grant that application until the issue has been determined and
-- any resulting order or notice complied with"; Article 20(1)(c): the court may order "that the entity must not be registered as a charity". Neither is among the six matters.
-- Reading A: the bars displace the duty to register (a court order first, because it is not temporary). Reading B: Article 11(4) prevails. Reading C: the model refuses to choose.
@ref Articles 19(9)(c) and 20(1)(c) (src:502) (src:517)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Articles 11(4), 19(9)(c) and 20(1)(c) conflict and this encoding does not choose between them` MEANS
    REFUSE "Articles 11(4), 19(9)(c) and 20(1)(c) conflict and this encoding does not choose between them"

-- src:502 | (c) must not, in the case of an application for registration, grant that application until the issue has been determined and any resulting order or notice complied with;
-- src:517 | (c) an order that the entity must not be registered as a charity;
@ref Articles 19(9)(c) and 20(1)(c) (src:502) (src:517)
GIVEN before IS A `Duty of the Commissioner on an application for registration` @desc The duty before the bars on granting are considered
      `Article 19(9)(c) bars granting the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a reported fitness issue is undetermined, or its resulting order or notice has not been complied with
      `the court has ordered that the entity must not be registered as a charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has made an order under Article 20(1)(c)
GIVETH A `Duty of the Commissioner on an application for registration`
DECIDE `F4.4 reading A: a bar on granting the application displaces the duty to register` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (before EQUALS `the Commissioner must register the applicant`) THEN before
        IF `the court has ordered that the entity must not be registered as a charity` THEN `the Commissioner must not register the applicant`
        IF `Article 19(9)(c) bars granting the application` THEN `the Commissioner must not yet grant the application`
        OTHERWISE before

-- src:502 | (c) must not, in the case of an application for registration, grant that application until the issue has been determined and any resulting order or notice complied with;
-- src:517 | (c) an order that the entity must not be registered as a charity;
@ref Articles 19(9)(c) and 20(1)(c) (src:502) (src:517)
GIVEN before IS A `Duty of the Commissioner on an application for registration` @desc The duty before the bars on granting are considered
GIVETH A `Duty of the Commissioner on an application for registration`
DECIDE `F4.4 reading B: the duty to register prevails once its six matters hold` IS before

-- src:502 | (c) must not, in the case of an application for registration, grant that application until the issue has been determined and any resulting order or notice complied with;
-- src:517 | (c) an order that the entity must not be registered as a charity;
@ref Articles 19(9)(c) and 20(1)(c) (src:502) (src:517)
GIVEN before IS A `Duty of the Commissioner on an application for registration` @desc The duty before the bars on granting are considered
      `Article 19(9)(c) bars granting the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a reported fitness issue is undetermined, or its resulting order or notice has not been complied with
      `the court has ordered that the entity must not be registered as a charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has made an order under Article 20(1)(c)
GIVETH A `Duty of the Commissioner on an application for registration`
DECIDE `F4.4 reading C: the duty to register and the bars conflict and the model refuses` IS
    IF     before EQUALS `the Commissioner must register the applicant`
       AND (   `Article 19(9)(c) bars granting the application`
            OR `the court has ordered that the entity must not be registered as a charity` )
    THEN `Articles 11(4), 19(9)(c) and 20(1)(c) conflict and this encoding does not choose between them`
    ELSE before

-- src:319 | (4) If the applicant complies with paragraph (2), with any Regulations under paragraph (3), and with Article 19(5), the Commissioner must register the applicant as a charity if satisfied that –
-- src:328 | (5) If not so satisfied, the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant.
@ref Article 11(4) and (5) (src:319) (src:328)
@export What the Commissioner must or must not do with the application: register the applicant (Article 11(4)), refuse to register (Article 11(5)), not yet grant it or not register it (Articles 19(9)(c), 20(1)(c)), or nothing yet because the application does not comply; on the readings given
GIVEN
  interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 11 and 12` @desc The reading of each ambiguity of Articles 11 and 12; a field left out takes the reading the encoding takes (see the fork register in FRAGMENT-G4.md)
  `the application` IS AN `Application for registration` @desc What the applicant has provided under Article 11(2), with the day it was lodged and the day, if any, it became complete
  `an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an Order under Article 13(9)(b) requires a registered charity to give a statement of its intentions about payments to governors; Article 11(2)(e)(ii) reads it of the applicant as it would be once registered
  `the applicant has complied with Article 19(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the application states that the entity holds declarations from all its governors who have not made a report under Article 19(2)
  `the entity` IS AN Entity @desc The applicant as Article 2 leaves it: its kinds of entity, whether it is a Jersey entity, its governors and its purposes
  `the entity meets the charity test` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 5: whether the applicant meets the charity test now
  `the findings` IS A `Findings of the Commissioner for Article 11(4)` @desc The Commissioner's findings on the matters of Article 11(4) that no other group decides, and on the grounds prescribed under Article 11(7)
  `the entity has a principal address in Jersey within Article 8(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the applicant has a principal address in Jersey within the meaning of Article 8(4)
  `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the name of the applicant is, in the Commissioner's opinion, undesirable as the registered name of a charity on a ground in Article 12(1)(a) to (d)
  `Article 19(9)(c) bars granting the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a reported fitness issue about a governor is undetermined, or its resulting order or notice has not been complied with
  `the court has ordered that the entity must not be registered as a charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has made an order under Article 20(1)(c) that the entity must not be registered as a charity
GIVETH A `Duty of the Commissioner on an application for registration`
DECIDE `Art 11 the duty of the Commissioner on the application` IS
    CONSIDER interp's `how the duty to register meets the bars on granting the application`
    WHEN `a bar on granting the application displaces the duty to register` THEN `F4.4 reading A: a bar on granting the application displaces the duty to register` before `Article 19(9)(c) bars granting the application` `the court has ordered that the entity must not be registered as a charity`
    WHEN `the duty to register prevails once its six matters hold` THEN `F4.4 reading B: the duty to register prevails once its six matters hold` before
    WHEN `the duty to register and the bars conflict and the model refuses` THEN `F4.4 reading C: the duty to register and the bars conflict and the model refuses` before `Article 19(9)(c) bars granting the application` `the court has ordered that the entity must not be registered as a charity`
    WHERE
        before MEANS `Art 11 the duty before the bars on granting` interp `the application` `an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity` `the applicant has complied with Article 19(5)` `the entity` `the entity meets the charity test` `the findings` `the entity has a principal address in Jersey within Article 8(4)` `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1)` `Article 19(9)(c) bars granting the application` `the court has ordered that the entity must not be registered as a charity`

-- The Commissioner's decisions that other provisions name (IP27): the subject is the decision "whether to register an applicant"; the outcome is "does what was sought" (registers) or "refuses". The other three
-- duties are not decisions and answer NOTHING; the Law says nothing about notifying an applicant of a refusal under Article 11 (Article 11(8)(a)(ii) lets an Order do so).
-- src:319 | (4) If the applicant complies with paragraph (2), with any Regulations under paragraph (3), and with Article 19(5), the Commissioner must register the applicant as a charity if satisfied that –
-- src:328 | (5) If not so satisfied, the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant.
@ref Article 11(4) and (5) (src:319) (src:328)
@export The decision of the Commissioner on the application as other provisions name it (the decision under Article 11 on whether to register a charity): that the Commissioner registers, or refuses; NOTHING where neither duty arises
GIVEN
  interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 11 and 12` @desc The reading of each ambiguity of Articles 11 and 12; a field left out takes the reading the encoding takes (see the fork register in FRAGMENT-G4.md)
  `the application` IS AN `Application for registration` @desc What the applicant has provided under Article 11(2), with the day it was lodged and the day, if any, it became complete
  `an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an Order under Article 13(9)(b) requires a registered charity to give a statement of its intentions about payments to governors; Article 11(2)(e)(ii) reads it of the applicant as it would be once registered
  `the applicant has complied with Article 19(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the application states that the entity holds declarations from all its governors who have not made a report under Article 19(2)
  `the entity` IS AN Entity @desc The applicant as Article 2 leaves it: its kinds of entity, whether it is a Jersey entity, its governors and its purposes
  `the entity meets the charity test` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 5: whether the applicant meets the charity test now
  `the findings` IS A `Findings of the Commissioner for Article 11(4)` @desc The Commissioner's findings on the matters of Article 11(4) that no other group decides, and on the grounds prescribed under Article 11(7)
  `the entity has a principal address in Jersey within Article 8(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the applicant has a principal address in Jersey within the meaning of Article 8(4)
  `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the name of the applicant is, in the Commissioner's opinion, undesirable as the registered name of a charity on a ground in Article 12(1)(a) to (d)
  `Article 19(9)(c) bars granting the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a reported fitness issue about a governor is undetermined, or its resulting order or notice has not been complied with
  `the court has ordered that the entity must not be registered as a charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has made an order under Article 20(1)(c) that the entity must not be registered as a charity
GIVETH A MAYBE `Decision of the Commissioner`
DECIDE `Art 11 what the Commissioner must do on the application` IS
    CONSIDER `Art 11 the duty of the Commissioner on the application` interp `the application` `an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity` `the applicant has complied with Article 19(5)` `the entity` `the entity meets the charity test` `the findings` `the entity has a principal address in Jersey within Article 8(4)` `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1)` `Article 19(9)(c) bars granting the application` `the court has ordered that the entity must not be registered as a charity`
    WHEN `the Commissioner must register the applicant` THEN JUST (`Decision of the Commissioner` OF `whether to register an applicant, Article 11`, `the Commissioner does what was sought or proposed`)
    WHEN `the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant` THEN JUST (`Decision of the Commissioner` OF `whether to register an applicant, Article 11`, `the Commissioner refuses`)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:319 | (4) If the applicant complies with paragraph (2), with any Regulations under paragraph (3), and with Article 19(5), the Commissioner must register the applicant as a charity if satisfied that –
@ref Article 11(4) (src:319)
DECIDE `the Commissioner registers the applicant` IS `Act under Article 11` OF `the Commissioner`, `register the applicant as a charity`

-- src:328 | (5) If not so satisfied, the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant.
@ref Article 11(5) (src:328)
DECIDE `the Commissioner refuses to register the applicant` IS `Act under Article 11` OF `the Commissioner`, `refuse to register the applicant`

-- src:319 | (4) If the applicant complies with paragraph (2), with any Regulations under paragraph (3), and with Article 19(5), the Commissioner must register the applicant as a charity if satisfied that –
@ref Article 11(4) (src:319)
@export The duty of the Commissioner to register the applicant as a charity (Article 11(4)): arises when the applicant complies and the six matters are found, unless a bar on granting displaces it, on the readings given; FULFILLED where it does not arise
GIVEN
  interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 11 and 12` @desc The reading of each ambiguity of Articles 11 and 12; a field left out takes the reading the encoding takes (see the fork register in FRAGMENT-G4.md)
  `the application` IS AN `Application for registration` @desc What the applicant has provided under Article 11(2), with the day it was lodged and the day, if any, it became complete
  `an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an Order under Article 13(9)(b) requires a registered charity to give a statement of its intentions about payments to governors; Article 11(2)(e)(ii) reads it of the applicant as it would be once registered
  `the applicant has complied with Article 19(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the application states that the entity holds declarations from all its governors who have not made a report under Article 19(2)
  `the entity` IS AN Entity @desc The applicant as Article 2 leaves it: its kinds of entity, whether it is a Jersey entity, its governors and its purposes
  `the entity meets the charity test` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 5: whether the applicant meets the charity test now
  `the findings` IS A `Findings of the Commissioner for Article 11(4)` @desc The Commissioner's findings on the matters of Article 11(4) that no other group decides, and on the grounds prescribed under Article 11(7)
  `the entity has a principal address in Jersey within Article 8(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the applicant has a principal address in Jersey within the meaning of Article 8(4)
  `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the name of the applicant is, in the Commissioner's opinion, undesirable as the registered name of a charity on a ground in Article 12(1)(a) to (d)
  `Article 19(9)(c) bars granting the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a reported fitness issue about a governor is undetermined, or its resulting order or notice has not been complied with
  `the court has ordered that the entity must not be registered as a charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has made an order under Article 20(1)(c) that the entity must not be registered as a charity
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 11`
DECIDE `Art 11(4) the Commissioner must register the applicant` IS
    IF `Art 11 the duty of the Commissioner on the application` interp `the application` `an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity` `the applicant has complied with Article 19(5)` `the entity` `the entity meets the charity test` `the findings` `the entity has a principal address in Jersey within Article 8(4)` `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1)` `Article 19(9)(c) bars granting the application` `the court has ordered that the entity must not be registered as a charity` EQUALS `the Commissioner must register the applicant`
    THEN PARTY `the Commissioner`
         MUST `the Commissioner registers the applicant`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

