§§§ `Article 11(6) -- guidance on a substantial activity`

-- src:329 | (6) For the purpose of paragraph (4)(c)(ii) –
-- src:330 | (a) the Commissioner must publish and maintain guidance as to how he or she determines whether an activity is substantial;
@ref Article 11(6)(a) (src:329-330)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 11`
DECIDE `Art 11(6)(a) the Commissioner must publish and maintain guidance on whether an activity is substantial` IS
    PARTY `the Commissioner`
    MUST `Act under Article 11` OF `the Commissioner`, `publish and maintain guidance on whether an activity is substantial`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- (b): "Articles 5(6) to (8) apply to that guidance as they apply to guidance under Article 5(4)". Group G2 encodes Article 5(6) to (8) for the guidance on the charity test and a group module may not call another group's,
-- so the three duties are restated here for this guidance, each with the cross-reference as its @ref. Article 5(6) obliges the Commissioner BEFORE issuing or amending guidance; Article 5(7) "within a reasonable time"
-- after issuing or amending it; Article 5(8) obliges the Minister "as soon as practicable" after receiving it. The Law gives no number of days: the default reading (F4.10) takes each as a determination the caller supplies.
-- src:331 | (b) Articles 5(6) to (8) apply to that guidance as they apply to guidance under Article 5(4);
-- src:158 | (6) Before issuing or amending guidance the Commissioner must –
-- src:159 | (a) consult –
-- src:160 | (i) any persons appearing to the Commissioner to be representative of charities or bodies with charitable purposes,
-- src:161 | (ii) the Minister, and
-- src:162 | (iii) such other persons as the Commissioner considers appropriate; and
-- src:163 | (b) publish a report on the Commissioner’s views on the results of the consultation, and the reasons for the Commissioner’s decision on the guidance in the light of those results.
@ref Article 11(6)(b) applying Article 5(6) (src:331) (src:158-163)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 11`
DECIDE `Art 11(6)(b) before issuing or amending the guidance the Commissioner must consult and publish a report` IS
    PARTY `the Commissioner`
    MUST `Act under Article 11` OF `the Commissioner`, `consult, and publish a report on the consultation, before issuing or amending the guidance`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:331 | (b) Articles 5(6) to (8) apply to that guidance as they apply to guidance under Article 5(4);
-- src:158 | (6) Before issuing or amending guidance the Commissioner must –
-- src:159 | (a) consult –
-- src:160 | (i) any persons appearing to the Commissioner to be representative of charities or bodies with charitable purposes,
-- src:161 | (ii) the Minister, and
-- src:162 | (iii) such other persons as the Commissioner considers appropriate; and
-- src:163 | (b) publish a report on the Commissioner’s views on the results of the consultation, and the reasons for the Commissioner’s decision on the guidance in the light of those results.
@ref Article 11(6)(b) applying Article 5(6) (src:331) (src:158-163)
GIVEN `the Commissioner consulted persons appearing to the Commissioner to be representative of charities or bodies with charitable purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 5(6)(a)(i)
      `the Commissioner consulted the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 5(6)(a)(ii)
      `the Commissioner consulted such other persons as the Commissioner considers appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 5(6)(a)(iii): the Commissioner's consideration of who is appropriate is a discretion, so this is an input
      `the Commissioner published a report on the Commissioner's views on the results of the consultation and the reasons for the decision on the guidance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 5(6)(b)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 11(6)(b) the consultation and the report are as Article 5(6) requires` IF
        `the Commissioner consulted persons appearing to the Commissioner to be representative of charities or bodies with charitable purposes`
    AND `the Commissioner consulted the Minister`
    AND `the Commissioner consulted such other persons as the Commissioner considers appropriate`
    AND `the Commissioner published a report on the Commissioner's views on the results of the consultation and the reasons for the decision on the guidance`

@ref Article 5(7) as applied by Article 11(6)(b) (src:164)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`no number of days for a reasonable time after issuing or amending the guidance is in the Law` MEANS
    REFUSE "no number of days for a reasonable time after issuing or amending the guidance is in the Law"

@ref Article 5(8) as applied by Article 11(6)(b) (src:165)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`no number of days for as soon as practicable after the Minister receives the guidance is in the Law` MEANS
    REFUSE "no number of days for as soon as practicable after the Minister receives the guidance is in the Law"

-- F4.10, Article 5(7): "Within a reasonable time after issuing or amending guidance the Commissioner must provide to the Minister a copy".
-- src:164 | (7) Within a reasonable time after issuing or amending guidance the Commissioner must provide to the Minister a copy of the issued or amended guidance and the report published under paragraph (6)(b).
@ref Article 5(7) as applied by Article 11(6)(b) (src:164)
GIVEN `the Commissioner provided the copy within a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The caller's determination that the Commissioner provided the copy within a reasonable time
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `F4.10 reading A: the copy was provided within a reasonable time` IS `the Commissioner provided the copy within a reasonable time`

-- src:164 | (7) Within a reasonable time after issuing or amending guidance the Commissioner must provide to the Minister a copy of the issued or amended guidance and the report published under paragraph (6)(b).
@ref Article 5(7) as applied by Article 11(6)(b) (src:164)
GIVEN `the day the guidance was issued or amended` IS A DATE @desc The day on which the guidance was issued or amended
      `the day the Commissioner provided the copy` IS A DATE @desc The day on which the Commissioner provided the copy to the Minister
      `the number of days that counts as a reasonable time` IS A MAYBE NUMBER @desc The number of days that counts as a reasonable time; NOTHING where none is given, which the Law does not do
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `F4.10 reading B: the copy was provided within the number of days` IS
    CONSIDER `the number of days that counts as a reasonable time`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `no number of days for a reasonable time after issuing or amending the guidance is in the Law`
    WHEN JUST allowance THEN (`the day the Commissioner provided the copy` MINUS `the day the guidance was issued or amended`) AT MOST allowance

-- src:164 | (7) Within a reasonable time after issuing or amending guidance the Commissioner must provide to the Minister a copy of the issued or amended guidance and the report published under paragraph (6)(b).
@ref Article 5(7) as applied by Article 11(6)(b) (src:164)
@export Whether the Commissioner provided the Minister with a copy of the guidance and the report within a reasonable time after issuing or amending it (Article 5(7) as applied by Article 11(6)(b)), on the reading given
GIVEN
  interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 11 and 12` @desc The reading of each ambiguity of Articles 11 and 12; a field left out takes the reading the encoding takes (see the fork register in FRAGMENT-G4.md)
  `the Commissioner provided the copy within a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The caller's determination that the Commissioner provided the copy within a reasonable time; used on the first reading only
  `the day the guidance was issued or amended` IS A DATE @desc The day on which the guidance was issued or amended; used on the second reading only
  `the day the Commissioner provided the copy` IS A DATE @desc The day on which the Commissioner provided the copy to the Minister; used on the second reading only
  `the number of days that counts as a reasonable time` IS A MAYBE NUMBER @desc The number of days that counts as a reasonable time; used on the second reading only
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 11(6)(b) the copy was provided to the Minister within a reasonable time` IF
    CONSIDER interp's `how reasonable time and as soon as practicable are read for the guidance`
    WHEN `as a determination the caller supplies` THEN `F4.10 reading A: the copy was provided within a reasonable time` `the Commissioner provided the copy within a reasonable time`
    WHEN `as a number of days from the event` THEN `F4.10 reading B: the copy was provided within the number of days` `the day the guidance was issued or amended` `the day the Commissioner provided the copy` `the number of days that counts as a reasonable time`

-- src:331 | (b) Articles 5(6) to (8) apply to that guidance as they apply to guidance under Article 5(4);
-- src:164 | (7) Within a reasonable time after issuing or amending guidance the Commissioner must provide to the Minister a copy of the issued or amended guidance and the report published under paragraph (6)(b).
@ref Article 11(6)(b) applying Article 5(7) (src:331) (src:164)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 11`
DECIDE `Art 11(6)(b) the Commissioner must provide the Minister with a copy of the guidance and the report` IS
    PARTY `the Commissioner`
    MUST `Act under Article 11` OF `the Commissioner`, `provide the Minister with a copy of the guidance and the report`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- F4.10, Article 5(8): "The Minister must lay a copy of the guidance and report so provided before the States as soon as practicable after the Minister receives the guidance and report."
-- src:165 | (8) The Minister must lay a copy of the guidance and report so provided before the States as soon as practicable after the Minister receives the guidance and report.
@ref Article 5(8) as applied by Article 11(6)(b) (src:165)
GIVEN `the Minister laid the copy as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The caller's determination that the Minister laid the copy before the States as soon as practicable
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `F4.10 reading A: the copy was laid as soon as practicable` IS `the Minister laid the copy as soon as practicable`

-- src:165 | (8) The Minister must lay a copy of the guidance and report so provided before the States as soon as practicable after the Minister receives the guidance and report.
@ref Article 5(8) as applied by Article 11(6)(b) (src:165)
GIVEN `the day the Minister received the guidance and the report` IS A DATE @desc The day on which the Minister received them
      `the day the Minister laid the copy before the States` IS A DATE @desc The day on which the Minister laid the copy before the States
      `the number of days that counts as as soon as practicable` IS A MAYBE NUMBER @desc The number of days that counts as as soon as practicable; NOTHING where none is given, which the Law does not do
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `F4.10 reading B: the copy was laid within the number of days` IS
    CONSIDER `the number of days that counts as as soon as practicable`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `no number of days for as soon as practicable after the Minister receives the guidance is in the Law`
    WHEN JUST allowance THEN (`the day the Minister laid the copy before the States` MINUS `the day the Minister received the guidance and the report`) AT MOST allowance

-- src:165 | (8) The Minister must lay a copy of the guidance and report so provided before the States as soon as practicable after the Minister receives the guidance and report.
@ref Article 5(8) as applied by Article 11(6)(b) (src:165)
@export Whether the Minister laid a copy of the guidance and the report before the States as soon as practicable after receiving them (Article 5(8) as applied by Article 11(6)(b)), on the reading given
GIVEN
  interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 11 and 12` @desc The reading of each ambiguity of Articles 11 and 12; a field left out takes the reading the encoding takes (see the fork register in FRAGMENT-G4.md)
  `the Minister laid the copy as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The caller's determination that the Minister laid the copy as soon as practicable; used on the first reading only
  `the day the Minister received the guidance and the report` IS A DATE @desc The day on which the Minister received them; used on the second reading only
  `the day the Minister laid the copy before the States` IS A DATE @desc The day on which the Minister laid the copy before the States; used on the second reading only
  `the number of days that counts as as soon as practicable` IS A MAYBE NUMBER @desc The number of days that counts as as soon as practicable; used on the second reading only
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 11(6)(b) the Minister laid the copy before the States as soon as practicable` IF
    CONSIDER interp's `how reasonable time and as soon as practicable are read for the guidance`
    WHEN `as a determination the caller supplies` THEN `F4.10 reading A: the copy was laid as soon as practicable` `the Minister laid the copy as soon as practicable`
    WHEN `as a number of days from the event` THEN `F4.10 reading B: the copy was laid within the number of days` `the day the Minister received the guidance and the report` `the day the Minister laid the copy before the States` `the number of days that counts as as soon as practicable`

