DECIDE `Art 11(6)(c) the Commissioner must have regard to the guidance in determining whether an activity is substantial` IS
    PARTY `the Commissioner`
    MUST `Act under Article 11` OF `the Commissioner`, `have regard to the guidance in determining whether an activity is substantial`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- (d): "a registered charity, a governor of a registered charity, the tribunal and the court must have regard to the guidance when performing any of their functions under this Law to which the guidance is relevant."
-- One rule, typed by the party: the four roles the paragraph names are bound, any other role is not. Whether the guidance is relevant to the function is an input.
-- src:333 | (d) a registered charity, a governor of a registered charity, the tribunal and the court must have regard to the guidance when performing any of their functions under this Law to which the guidance is relevant.
@ref Article 11(6)(d) (src:333)
GIVEN party IS A `Legal actor` @desc The party in question
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 11(6)(d) the paragraph binds the party` IF
    CONSIDER party
    WHEN `a registered charity` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a governor` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Charity Tribunal` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the court` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- src:333 | (d) a registered charity, a governor of a registered charity, the tribunal and the court must have regard to the guidance when performing any of their functions under this Law to which the guidance is relevant.
@ref Article 11(6)(d) (src:333)
GIVEN party IS A `Legal actor` @desc The party in question: a registered charity, a governor of a registered charity, the tribunal or the court
      `the guidance is relevant to a function the party is performing under this Law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the guidance is relevant to a function the party is performing
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 11`
DECIDE `Art 11(6)(d) the party must have regard to the guidance` IS
    IF     `Art 11(6)(d) the paragraph binds the party` party
       AND `the guidance is relevant to a function the party is performing under this Law`
    THEN PARTY party
         MUST `Act under Article 11` OF party, `have regard to the guidance when performing a function to which it is relevant`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§§ `Article 11(7) -- further grounds of refusal`

-- src:334 | (7) The States may by Regulations prescribe further grounds on which an application must or may be refused, and those grounds may, without limitation, include –
@ref Article 11(7) (src:334)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 11`
DECIDE `Art 11(7) the States may prescribe further grounds on which an application must or may be refused` IS
    PARTY `the States`
    MAY `Act under Article 11` OF `the States`, `make Regulations prescribing further grounds on which an application must or may be refused`

-- (a) and (b) are examples the Regulations "may, without limitation, include". No Regulations are among the sources, so they are encoded as the tests the Regulations would apply if they adopted them,
-- and nothing in Article 11(4)(f) calls them: the input of (f) is whether a prescribed ground applies or should be applied.
-- src:335 | (a) that the entity has only one governor, not being a person who, by way of acting as a governor, carries on a prescribed description of regulated financial services business or any other prescribed description of business; or
@ref Article 11(7)(a) (src:335)
GIVEN
  `the entity` IS AN Entity @desc The applicant as Article 2 leaves it: its kinds of entity, whether it is a Jersey entity, its governors and its purposes
  `the sole governor, by way of acting as a governor, carries on a prescribed description of regulated financial services business or any other prescribed description of business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the only governor, by way of acting as a governor, carries on a description of business that the Regulations prescribe
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 11(7)(a) the entity has only one governor who does not carry on a prescribed description of business as a governor` IF
        count (`the entity`'s governors) EQUALS 1
    AND NOT `the sole governor, by way of acting as a governor, carries on a prescribed description of regulated financial services business or any other prescribed description of business`

-- src:336 | (b) that a number or proportion of its governors are related to each other in prescribed ways.
@ref Article 11(7)(b) (src:336)
GIVEN `a number or proportion of the governors are related to each other in a way that the Regulations prescribe` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a number or proportion of the entity's governors are related to each other in a way, and in a number or proportion, that the Regulations prescribe
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 11(7)(b) a number or proportion of the governors are related to each other in prescribed ways` IF
    `a number or proportion of the governors are related to each other in a way that the Regulations prescribe`

§§§ `Article 11(9) -- certificates of registration`

-- (a): "on registering an entity as a charity, issue to that charity a certificate of registration ... confirming the registered name, the registration number and the date of registration of the charity".
-- The certificate is the act, and carries the three things it confirms; the Law gives no time for issuing it.
-- src:344 | (9) The Commissioner must –
-- src:345 | (a) on registering an entity as a charity, issue to that charity a certificate of registration, in the form published by the Commissioner, confirming the registered name, the registration number and the date of registration of the charity; and
@ref Article 11(9)(a) (src:344-345)
@export The duty of the Commissioner, on registering an entity as a charity, to issue it a certificate confirming the registered name, the registration number and the date of registration (Article 11(9)(a)); FULFILLED where the entity has not been registered
GIVEN `the Commissioner has registered the entity as a charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has registered the entity as a charity
      `the registered charity` IS A `Registered charity` @desc What the register holds about the charity: its registered name, registration number and date of registration
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 11`
DECIDE `Art 11(9)(a) the Commissioner must issue a certificate of registration` IS
    IF `the Commissioner has registered the entity as a charity`
    THEN PARTY `the Commissioner`
         MUST `Act under Article 11` OF `the Commissioner`, (`issue a certificate of registration` (`the registered charity`'s `registered name`) (`the registered charity`'s `registration number`) (`the registered charity`'s `date registered`))
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- (b): "on entering on the register a new or alternative registered name, under Article 12(5), issue a further such certificate confirming the new or alternative registered name and the date on which that name was entered".
-- src:344 | (9) The Commissioner must –
-- src:346 | (b) on entering on the register a new or alternative registered name, under Article 12(5), issue a further such certificate confirming the new or alternative registered name and the date on which that name was entered on the register.
@ref Article 11(9)(b) (src:344) (src:346)
@export The duty of the Commissioner, on entering on the register a new or alternative registered name under Article 12(5), to issue a further certificate confirming that name and the date on which it was entered (Article 11(9)(b)); FULFILLED where no such name has been entered
GIVEN `the Commissioner has entered a new or alternative registered name under Article 12(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has entered a new or alternative registered name on the register
      `the new or alternative registered name` IS A STRING @desc The name that was entered
      `the day on which that name was entered on the register` IS A DATE @desc The day on which the name was entered on the register
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 11`
DECIDE `Art 11(9)(b) the Commissioner must issue a further certificate for a new or alternative registered name` IS
    IF `the Commissioner has entered a new or alternative registered name under Article 12(5)`
    THEN PARTY `the Commissioner`
         MUST `Act under Article 11` OF `the Commissioner`, (`issue a further certificate for a new or alternative registered name` `the new or alternative registered name` `the day on which that name was entered on the register`)
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED
